{"raw": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=06849628-1ff9-4555-9b68-cb637d20bae8&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201862129258_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "ACCOMPANIST", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-25\n\nLocation: Lindsborg\n\nBethany College Lindsborg, Kansas Bethany College ACCOMPANIST FLSA Status: HOURLY, NON-EXEMPT Department: Music Reports to: Academic Dean/CAO Positions Managed: None Why Bethany: Rooted in our Lutheran heritage and the transformative power of the liberal arts, Bethany prepares students to lead lives of purpose, leadership, creativity, and service in a complex and changing world. Located in Lindsborg, Kansas\u2014affectionately known as \"Little Sweden\" and celebrated for its vibrant arts community\u2014Bethany offers a close-knit environment where faculty and staff know students by name and mentor them in a highly personalized setting.\u00a0 Education at Bethany is rooted in intellectual discovery and a deep sense of belonging, equipping students to think critically, lead ethically, and serve with purpose. As a small, private, rural college, Bethany plays an essential role in renewing civic life, expanding opportunity, and fostering community revitalization. We believe in the value of personalized liberal arts education, the power of community, and the promise of rural America.\u00a0 At Bethany, you'll have the opportunity to inspire the next generation while contributing to the cultural and academic life of our campus and region as we prepare students to make meaningful contributions to the world. At Bethany, you'll have the opportunity to inspire the next generation while contributing to the cultural and academic life of our campus and region as we prepare students to make meaningful contributions to the world. About Bethany College: Founded in 1881, Bethany College is a dynamic liberal arts institution located in Lindsborg, Kansas\u2014known as \u201cLittle Sweden U.S.A.\u201d Bethany provides a transformative educational experience grounded in faith, learning, and community. The College is dedicated to cultivating leaders who serve and inspire through integrity, creativity, and purpose. Position Overview: The Staff Accompanist contributes to the artistic and faith life of the College through performances, institutional events, and technical support for Music Department concerts, programs, and the Office of Spiritual Life. This position provides collaborative piano support for the vocal and choral programs at Bethany College and works closely with music faculty, choral directors, and students to support rehearsals, performances, lessons, juried evaluations, chapel services, and special events during the academic year.\u00a0 Essential Functions: Applied Lesson Support Accompany voice lessons as assigned by the voice faculty. Accompany student recitals, including degree recitals and studio recitals. Collaborate with voice students in preparation for auditions and competitions, including NATS-sponsored events. Student Recruitment and Academic Evaluations Accompany prospective students during auditions and recruiting events for the Music program. Accompany students during end-of-semester vocal juries. Support students during recital hearings and performance assessments. Opera and Musical Theatre Serve as rehearsal and performance accompanist for departmental musical theatre or opera productions as assigned. Participate in music rehearsals and production preparation as required. Office of Spiritual Life In tandem with music faculty, serve as collaborative pianist for annual events associated with the Bethany College Messiah Festival of the Arts. Provide accompaniment for guest artist recitals when needed. Participate in master classes with visiting artists. Provide piano music for weekly chapel services and a chapel singing group as needed. Assist with event setup for music-related programs for the Office of Spiritual Life as needed.\u00a0 The statements contained herein describe the scope of responsibility and essential functions of this position, but should not be considered an all-inclusive listing of work requirements. Individuals may perform other duties as assigned, including work in other areas to cover absences or provide relief to equalize peak work periods or otherwise balance the workload.\u00a0 Qualifications: Required: Demonstrated experience accompanying vocal repertoire and choral ensembles. Strong sight-reading skills and familiarity with vocal and choral literature. Ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, students, and guest artists. Excellent grammar, spelling, and writing abilities. Microsoft Office, computer knowledge, and knowledge of office equipment. Ability to communicate effectively to a variety of audiences, including students, parents, faculty, staff, alumni, administration, and the community-at-large. Ability to handle multiple projects and assignments concurrently and be very results-oriented. Highly motivated and works well both independently and in a team environment. Preferred: Associate\u2019s or Bachelor\u2019s degree in Collaborative Piano, Piano Performance, or a related field. Experience accompanying high school or collegiate vocal programs. Experience with opera, musical theatre, and oratorio repertoire. Experience accompanying competitions such as those sponsored by the National Association of Teachers of Singing (NATS). Experience operating livestream platforms and basic audio/video equipment for performances and events. Familiarity with sound reinforcement, microphone setup, and concert video recording in a recital or concert setting. Bilingual in Spanish is a plus, or some knowledge of the Spanish language is a plus Working Conditions: Average of 15 hours per week when classes are in session, with some additional hours for special events. Position totals 510 hours per academic year, spread across the academic calendar. Most hours occur during the regular workday, with some evenings and weekends required. Some travel may be required for specific events; approved event travel costs are covered. Commuting costs to campus are not reimbursed. Work is performed in rehearsal, performance, chapel, and campus event settings. Compensation\u00a0 Supportive, mission-driven community and a beautiful campus environment Hourly rate of $30.00 Total compensation of $15,300 per academic year This position is not eligible for benefits How to Apply: Apply online at Employment Submit resume and cover letter EEO: Bethany College, an institution of the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America (ELCA), provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, sex, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law.\u00a0 This policy reflects Bethany College's mission to educate, develop, and challenge individuals to reach for truth and excellence as they lead lives of faith, learning, and service. This commitment to equal employment opportunities strengthens our community and enhances our ability to fulfill our educational mission.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=06849628-1ff9-4555-9b68-cb637d20bae8&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201740395565_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "MBA Adjunct", "description": "Posted: 2025-11-09\n\nLocation: Lindsborg\n\nADJUNCT BUSINESS FACULTY (MBA Program) Bethany College, Lindsborg, Kansas Adjunct faculty members are sought to teach within our MBA Program, in person in Lindsborg, Kansas. A student-centered approach to teaching is required. The primary responsibilities are to teach graduate-level courses within the business discipline.\u00a0 The following courses require instructors, meet once per week, and are scheduled for the Spring 2026 semester: BU401 Ethics and the Law: Business and Society BU404 Management Information Systems BU609 Managerial Finance BU610 Strategic Planning This position resides within the Division of Business, Professional Schools. The division provides graduate education in business administration, culminating in a Masters of Business Administration (MBA) degree. All adjunct faculty members shall support the Bethany College Mission.\u00a0 Job Requirements: Ph.D. or terminal degree in related business curriculum preferred; ABD, or MBA with teaching and/or professional business experience will be considered.\u00a0 Conduct class sessions as scheduled. Highly motivated, works well both independently and in a team environment.\u202f\u00a0 Functional knowledge of the Microsoft Office Suite, and Canvas LMS.\u202f\u00a0 Willingness to adapt to a changing technological environment, and competent in electronic mail and document management.\u202f\u00a0 Maintain current, accurate records of course enrollment, grades, and attendance. Observe and evaluate student performance in meeting course objectives and student learning outcomes through assignments, facilitating students\u2019 learning by designing lessons, presentations, discussions, classroom field experiences, projects, and appropriate assessments.\u00a0 Distribute syllabi that fulfill the course requirements, and select appropriate course-related materials. Assign and provide feedback for in- and out-of-class work; monitor student progress. Perform related duties as assigned, including communicating with the department chair(s).\u00a0 The statements contained herein describe the scope of the responsibility and essential functions of this position, but should not be considered to be an all-inclusive listing of work requirements.\u00a0 Application Process Interested candidates should submit: Curriculum vitae Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Anticipated start date would be January 2026 for the spring semester. EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITIES: Bethany College provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, or genetics. In addition to federal law requirements, Bethany College complies with applicable state and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment in every location in which the company has facilities.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=06849628-1ff9-4555-9b68-cb637d20bae8&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201898542029_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Director of Admissions", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\n\nLocation: Lindsborg\n\nBethany College Lindsborg, Kansas Bethany College DIRECTOR OF ADMISSIONS MUST INCLUDE A RESUME AND A COVER LETTER FLSA Status: SALARY; EXEMPT Department:\u00a0 Admissions Reports to:\u00a0 Dean of Enrollment Why Bethany: Rooted in our Lutheran heritage and the transformative power of the liberal arts, Bethany prepares students to lead lives of purpose, leadership, creativity, and service in a complex and changing world. Located in Lindsborg, Kansas\u2014affectionately known as \"Little Sweden\" and celebrated for its vibrant arts community\u2014Bethany offers a close-knit environment where faculty and staff know students by name and mentor them in a highly personalized setting.\u00a0 Education at Bethany is rooted in intellectual discovery and a deep sense of belonging, equipping students to think critically, lead ethically, and serve with purpose. As a small, private, rural college, Bethany plays an essential role in renewing civic life, expanding opportunity, and fostering community revitalization.\u00a0 At Bethany, you'll have the opportunity to inspire the next generation while contributing to the cultural and academic life of our campus and region as we prepare students to make meaningful contributions to the world. About Bethany College: Founded in 1881, Bethany College is a dynamic liberal arts institution located in Lindsborg, Kansas\u2014known as \u201cLittle Sweden U.S.A.\u201d Bethany provides a transformative educational experience grounded in faith, learning, and community. The College is dedicated to cultivating leaders who serve and inspire through integrity, creativity, and purpose. Position Overview: Bethany College invites applications for a visionary, strategic, and action-oriented leader to serve as Director of Admissions . This is a pivotal opportunity for a collaborative professional who believes in the value of personalized liberal arts education, the power of community, and the promise of rural America. Reporting to the Dean of Enrollment, the Director of Admissions will lead the development and implementation of an innovative, relationship-driven, data-informed recruitment strategy designed to strengthen enrollment, shape a mission-fit incoming class, and advance Bethany\u2019s vision for the future. Essential Functions: Lead and inspire a team of admissions counselors and student ambassadors in the recruitment of first-year, transfer, and international students. Develop and implement territory management plans that align with institutional goals and respond to shifting market and demographic trends. Oversee the application process , including review, decision policy, and coordination with academic and student support partners and external service providers. Collaborate closely with Financial Aid, Athletics, Marketing, Academic Affairs, and key external partners in enrollment management to ensure a seamless and student-centered enrollment experience. Design and deliver impactful campus visit programs, virtual events, and yield strategies that reflect the college\u2019s warm, relational culture. Analyze enrollment data and CRM insights (experience with Slate preferred) to guide decision-making and measure impact. Represent Bethany College to prospective students, families, school counselors, and community organizations with authenticity, enthusiasm, and integrity. Partner in advancing Bethany\u2019s mission to educate students \u201cto live fulfilling lives, inspired by faith and love of learning.\u201d The statements contained herein describe the scope of responsibility and essential functions of this position, but should not be considered an all-inclusive listing of work requirements. Individuals may perform other duties as assigned, including work in other areas to cover absences or provide relief to equalize peak work periods or otherwise balance the workload.\u00a0 Qualifications: Required: Bachelor\u2019s degree required. At least five years of progressive experience in admissions, enrollment, or related areas, preferably at a small private or faith-based institution. Mastery of best practices in relational recruitment for a small, private college according to NACAC professional standards, and the ability to train others. Excellent communication skills and ability to lead teams, build cross-campus collaboration, and manage complex projects successfully with creativity and clarity. Strong skills in data analysis, enrollment trends, and CRM use. Experience with recruiting international students and managing immigration, student visas, and federally required reporting. Demonstrated understanding of the critical links among recruitment, retention, academic programs, discount strategy, and financial sustainability, especially in the context of a small private liberal arts college. Excellent grammar, spelling, and writing abilities\u00a0 Microsoft Office, computer knowledge, and knowledge of office equipment\u00a0 Ability to communicate effectively to a variety of audiences, including students, parents, faculty, staff, alumni, administration, and the community at large Ability to handle multiple projects/assignments concurrently and be very results-oriented Highly motivated and works well both independently and in a team environment Preferred: Master\u2019s degree. Slate experience preferred. Bilingual in Spanish is a plus, or some knowledge of the Spanish language is a plus Working Conditions: Regular and satisfactory attendance and punctuality. Office work is at Bethany College - Sit for long periods of time. On-site work is generally performed indoors, with ambient room temperatures, lighting, and traditional office equipment found in a typical office environment. Evenings and weekends may be required. Travel may be needed depending on the recruiting schedule Bend, squat, kneel, reach above shoulders, handle objects (dexterity), push/pull, carry/lift 25 lbs. Must be available to work weekend and evening hours, including home athletic events, and occasional travel may be required. Walking across campus and standing during events. Compensation & Benefits:\u00a0 Competitive salary commensurate with experience Comprehensive benefits package, including health, dental, vision, and retirement plans Generous vacation, sick leave, and holidays Tuition remission benefits Professional Development Funds Possible Relocation Assistance Opportunities for professional development and leadership growth Supportive, mission-driven community and a beautiful campus environment How to Apply: Apply online at Employment Submit resume, cover letter, and references EEO: Bethany College, an institution of the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America (ELCA), provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, sex, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law.\u00a0 This policy reflects Bethany College's mission to educate, develop, and challenge individuals to reach for truth and excellence as they lead lives of faith, learning, and service. This commitment to equal employment opportunities strengthens our community and enhances our ability to fulfill our educational mission.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=06849628-1ff9-4555-9b68-cb637d20bae8&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201901847174_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Asst Men's Basketball Coach & Game Mgmt", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\n\nLocation: Lindsborg\n\nBethany College Lindsborg, Kansas Bethany College ASSISTANT MEN\u2019S BASKETBALL COACH & GAME MANAGEMENT ASSISTANT MUST INCLUDE REFERENCES, RESUME AND A COVER LETTER FLSA Status: SALARY; EXEMPT Department:\u00a0 Athletics Reports to:\u00a0 Head Men\u2019s Basketball Coach (for Coaching duties); Dean of Athletics & Assistant Athletic Director (for Game Management & Departmental duties) Positions Managed:\u00a0 Student Workers (as authorized/approved) Why Bethany: Rooted in our Lutheran heritage and the transformative power of the liberal arts, Bethany prepares students to lead lives of purpose, leadership, creativity, and service in a complex and changing world. Located in Lindsborg, Kansas\u2014affectionately known as \"Little Sweden\" and celebrated for its vibrant arts community\u2014Bethany offers a close-knit environment where faculty and staff know students by name and mentor them in a highly personalized setting.\u00a0 Education at Bethany is rooted in intellectual discovery and a deep sense of belonging, equipping students to think critically, lead ethically, and serve with purpose. As a small, private, rural college, Bethany plays an essential role in renewing civic life, expanding opportunity, and fostering community revitalization. We believe in the value of personalized liberal arts education, the power of community, and the promise of rural America.\u00a0 At Bethany, you'll have the opportunity to inspire the next generation while contributing to the cultural and academic life of our campus and region as we prepare students to make meaningful contributions to the world. About Bethany College: \u00a0 Founded in 1881, Bethany College is a dynamic liberal arts institution located in Lindsborg, Kansas\u2014known as \u201cLittle Sweden U.S.A.\u201d Bethany provides a transformative educational experience grounded in faith, learning, and community. The College is dedicated to cultivating leaders who serve and inspire through integrity, creativity, and purpose. Position Overview: This dual-role position, under the direction of the Head Men\u2019s Basketball Coach and the Athletic Administration, is responsible for: 1. Assisting the Head Coach in coordinating a safe, enthusiastic, and competitive men\u2019s basketball program. 2. Recruiting, supervising, and coaching NAIA student-athletes in accordance with Bethany College, Kansas Collegiate Athletic Conference (KCAC), and National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA) regulations. 3. Serving as Game Management Assistant for home athletic contests to ensure events are administered efficiently, safely, and in alignment with College values. 4. Fostering both athletic and academic excellence, retention, and good sportsmanship across the student-athlete experience. Campus Housing Opportunity: On-campus housing is available for this position at the deeply discounted rate of $100 per month with payroll deduction. Essential Functions: Men\u2019s Basketball Coaching & Program Operations Assist in administering all phases of an NAIA men's basketball program, including active recruitment of qualified student-athletes adhering to the College recruitment scholarship model. Lead, support, and prioritize student retention, academic progress, and persistence to graduation. Create and foster a positive environment of growth, development, and support for student-athletes both in and out of competition. *(Hostile, demeaning, or derogatory coaching tactics are strictly prohibited).* Assist in planning, organizing, and conducting pre-season, in-season, and post-season conditioning, practices, and competitive games. Assist in formulating competitive game and practice schedules. Coordinate on-campus visits for recruits and their families. Arrange team travel, lodging, and meal logistics. Prepare and manage team records, travel expense statements, and trip itineraries. Lead community engagement and service-learning opportunities for the men\u2019s basketball program. Plan and lead individual development and goal-setting meetings with student-athletes. Assist in monitoring facility safety conditions, equipment inventory, and maintenance under the program's jurisdiction. Actively participate in fundraising initiatives for the basketball program and the Department of Athletics. Game Management & Event Administration Serve as the designated Game Manager for assigned home athletic contests across various sports. Oversee game-day environments, crowd control, and fan behavior to ensure a safe, welcoming, and positive atmosphere for student-athletes, officials, and spectators. Prepare facilities and locker rooms for visiting teams and game officials; provide escort and hospitality for officials. Support game-day operations staff and coordinate student workers (scheduling, task assignment, and training). Assist with concessions operations, including inventory, purchasing, volunteer/staff scheduling, and secure cash box balancing and bank deposits. Departmental Collaboration & Professional Standards Maintain strict adherence to all Bethany College, KCAC, and NAIA rules, regulations, and spending/budgeting policies. Participate actively in departmental meetings and contribute ideas to enhance operational efficiency. Collaborate professionally with campus academic divisions, student development, admissions, and administrative offices. Engage in ongoing professional development clinics, workshops, and conventions. The statements contained herein describe the scope of responsibility and essential functions of this position, but should not be considered an all-inclusive listing of work requirements. Individuals may perform other duties as assigned, including work in other areas to cover absences or provide relief to equalize peak work periods or otherwise balance the workload.\u00a0 Qualifications: Required: Bachelor\u2019s degree (B.A./B.S.) from an accredited four-year college or university, or equivalent combination of education and coaching experience. Demonstrated understanding of NAIA philosophy and the role of athletics in a faith-based, liberal arts environment. Excellent grammar, spelling, and writing abilities\u00a0 Microsoft Office, computer knowledge, and knowledge of office equipment\u00a0 Ability to communicate effectively to a variety of audiences, including students, parents, faculty, staff, alumni, administration, and the community-at-large Ability to handle multiple projects/assignments concurrently and be very results-oriented Highly motivated and works well both independently and in a team environment Regular, dependable attendance and punctuality Preferred: Collegiate playing or coaching experience (Men\u2019s Basketball). Experience with event management, athletic game administration, or facility oversight. Bilingual proficiency in Spanish (or conversational knowledge). Physical Skills and Abilities: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Ability to sit, stand, walk, run, and demonstrate basketball fundamentals/drills as needed during practice sessions. Walking primarily on indoor court surfaces and athletic grounds for extended periods. Reaching above shoulder height, bending below the waist, and lifting/moving equipment up to 40\u201350 lbs using proper lifting techniques. Good hand-eye coordination, dexterity, and visual acuity to evaluate athletic performance, use office computer equipment, and manage game-day setups. Working Conditions: Work Location: Athletic Complex & Bethany College Campus (Lindsborg, KS). Work Schedule: Irregular and extended hours, including frequent evenings, weekends, and holidays according to the athletic competition schedule. Travel: Frequent conference-wide (KCAC/NAIA) and regional travel required for games, tournaments, and recruiting. Environment: Indoor office and gymnasium environments with ambient temperatures, as well as occasional outdoor event oversight with exposure to varying seasonal weather elements, noise, and crowd conditions. Compensation & Benefits:\u00a0 Competitive salary commensurate with experience Comprehensive benefits package, including health, dental, vision, and retirement plans Generous vacation, sick leave, and holidays Tuition remission benefits Professional Development Funds Possible Relocation Assistance Opportunities for professional development and leadership growth Supportive, mission-driven community and a beautiful campus environment Housing Benefit: Dedicated on-campus housing is available to the employee at a reduced employee rate of $100 per month through payroll deduction. How to Apply: Apply online at Employment Submit references, resume and cover letter EEO: Bethany College, an institution of the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America (ELCA), provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, sex, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law.\u00a0 This policy reflects Bethany College's mission to educate, develop, and challenge individuals to reach for truth and excellence as they lead lives of faith, learning, and service. This commitment to equal employment opportunities strengthens our community and enhances our ability to fulfill our educational mission.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=06849628-1ff9-4555-9b68-cb637d20bae8&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201905879416_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "ADJUNCT OF EDUCATION", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Lindsborg\n\nBethany College Lindsborg, Kansas Bethany College To be considered for this position, please submit the following: a curriculum vitae, a Teaching Philosophy Statement, and References (transcripts will be required upon hire). EDUCATION ADJUNCT: MATH METHODS FLSA Status: \u00a0 Exempt, salary based on contract Position Type: \u00a0 Part-time, Non-Tenure Track Location & Modality: On the Bethany College campus in Lindsborg, Kansas (evening) or Hybrid (full-remote instruction is not being considered at this time) Schedule: Most commonly offered as an evening course to accommodate working professionals, with scheduling flexibility Department: \u00a0 Education Contact: Alan English, Education Department Chair, at Englishae@bethanylb.edu Appointment Time: \u00a0 Term:\u00a0Spring 2027 (SP27) Teaching Responsibilities: Teaching load:\u00a01 course\u00a0 Course Levels:\u00a0Undergraduate Specific Courses:\u00a0ED327 \u2013 Teaching Mathematics in the PreK\u2013Middle Level Classroom Early Alert System with Student Success\u00a0participation required Office Hours:\u00a0Scheduled as appropriate for student support Learning Management Systems:\u00a0Canvas Why Bethany: Bethany College invites applications for dynamic, student-centered professionals to join our vibrant community.\u00a0 Rooted in our Lutheran heritage and the transformative power of the liberal arts, Bethany prepares students to lead lives of purpose, leadership, creativity, and service in a complex and changing world. Located in Lindsborg, Kansas\u2014affectionately known as \"Little Sweden\" and celebrated for its vibrant arts community\u2014Bethany offers a close-knit environment where faculty and staff know students by name and mentor them in a highly personalized setting.\u00a0 Education at Bethany is rooted in intellectual discovery and a deep sense of belonging, equipping students to think critically, lead ethically, and serve with purpose. As a small, private, rural college, Bethany plays an essential role in renewing civic life, expanding opportunity, and fostering community revitalization. We believe in the value of personalized liberal arts education, the power of community, and the promise of rural America.\u00a0 At Bethany, you'll have the opportunity to inspire the next generation while contributing to the cultural and academic life of our campus and region as we prepare students to make meaningful contributions to the world. About Bethany College: Founded in 1881, Bethany College is a dynamic liberal arts institution located in Lindsborg, Kansas\u2014known as \u201cLittle Sweden U.S.A.\u201d Bethany provides a transformative educational experience grounded in faith, learning, and community. The College is dedicated to cultivating leaders who serve and inspire through integrity, creativity, and purpose. Position Overview: The Education Department at Bethany College seeks a dedicated, dynamic educator for an adjunct instructor position to teach ED327: Teaching Mathematics in the PreK\u2013Middle Level Classroom during the Spring 2027 (SP27) semester. This undergraduate methods course is a required core requirement for Elementary Education majors, typically taken during their junior year. ED327 Course Description: \u00a0A course for pre-service teachers designed to develop competencies in: Knowledge of developmentally appropriate standards-based curricula, Pedagogy to empower all students and direct them toward mathematical understanding, and Mathematical theory as it applies to current reform efforts. Modality & Scheduling Flexibility: Recognizing that many qualified adjunct candidates are active, full-time classroom teachers or educational practitioners, this position is offered primarily as an evening course to accommodate professional work schedules, with flexibility in meeting times. While on-campus instruction in Lindsborg is preferred, a hybrid delivery model (combining structured on-campus sessions with online components) is fully acceptable. Please note: Fully remote instruction is not being considered for this position at this time. An established syllabus is available to provide a strong structural foundation; however, the instructor is enthusiastically encouraged to bring their own professional expertise, classroom experiences, and instructional creativity to make the course their own. Bethany College Student Body: At Bethany College, you'll be teaching bright, purpose-driven students in a uniquely personal educational environment. Our student body thrives in our close-knit campus community located in Lindsborg, Kansas, where Swedish cultural heritage enriches the collegiate experience. Bethany students are characterized by their intellectual curiosity, active engagement in learning, and genuine desire to discover their true purpose. They value authentic relationships with faculty who recognize their individual stories, passions, and potential.\u00a0 As an educator here, you'll have the opportunity to truly know your students\u2014their dreams, their challenges, and their aspirations\u2014while guiding them through transformative learning experiences. Our Swedes eagerly embrace leadership opportunities, form lasting friendships, and develop the confidence to pursue fulfilling careers aligned with their purpose. They're not just preparing for jobs; they're developing into thoughtful citizens who will think, act, and live with purpose long after graduation, contributing meaningfully to their communities and the world. Essential Functions: Deliver high-quality, student-centered instruction for ED327 in either an on-campus evening or hybrid format. Prepare syllabi (or use prepared syllabi), course materials, lectures, learning activities, and assessments aligned with state and national mathematics education standards for PreK\u2013middle level teacher preparation. Utilize the college\u2019s Learning Management System (Canvas) for course delivery, grade recording, and communication. Provide timely, constructive feedback and evaluation on pre-service teacher assignments, lesson plans, and demonstrations. Maintain regular attendance, hold accessible office/consultation hours for students, and respond to student inquiries in a timely manner. Participate in the college\u2019s Student Success Early Alert System to identify and support students who may need academic assistance. Submit midterm and final course grades according to institutional deadlines and registrar guidelines. Maintain professional collaboration with the Education Department Chair and fellow faculty members. Qualifications: \u00a0Required: Master\u2019s degree in Education,\u00a0Mathematics Education, Curriculum & Instruction, or a closely related field. Relevant teaching experience in PreK\u2013middle level mathematics or teacher preparation. Good communication skills, organized, and able to perform multiple tasks simultaneously. Ability to communicate effectively to a variety of audiences, including students, parents, faculty, staff, alumni, administration, and the community-at-large. Ability to handle multiple projects/assignments concurrently and be very results-oriented.\u00a0 Highly motivated and works well both independently and in a team environment. Demonstrated ability to mentor and motivate students. Regular, dependable attendance and adherence to professional standards. Preferred: Current or previous state teaching certification/licensure in Elementary Education or Middle Level Mathematics. Familiarity with current mathematics reform efforts, NCTM standards, and state educator standards. Experience utilizing Learning Management Systems (e.g., Canvas) and educational technology tools. Competence in email, document management, and standard office/instructional software. Bilingual proficiency in Spanish (a plus). Functional knowledge of Microsoft Windows and Microsoft Office Basic personal computer operation Willingness to adapt to a changing technology environment, i.e. updates, security, and new versions Ability to use multiple Internet browsers Working Conditions Work performed indoors is with ambient room temperatures, lighting, and traditional classroom equipment\u00a0 On the campus of Bethany College, Lindsborg How to Apply: Apply online at Employment Curriculum vitae and cover letter Teaching philosophy statement References EEO: Bethany College, an institution of the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America (ELCA), provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, sex, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law.\u00a0 This policy reflects Bethany College's mission to educate, develop, and challenge individuals to reach for truth and excellence as they lead lives of faith, learning, and service. This commitment to equal employment opportunities strengthens our community and enhances our ability to fulfill our educational mission.", "department": ""}}, "rows": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=06849628-1ff9-4555-9b68-cb637d20bae8&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201862129258_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 466, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=06849628-1ff9-4555-9b68-cb637d20bae8&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201862129258_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "ACCOMPANIST", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-06-25", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=0